<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hernán Cortés</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cortés</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hernán Cortés was a Spanish conquistador who led the expedition that brought down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> between 1519 and 1521. Allied with indigenous peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlaxcalans">Tlaxcalans</a>, he captured the Aztec capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>. His conquest was a founding event of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes.jpg" alt="Hernán Cortés" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Hern%C3%A1n_Cort%C3%A9s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
